{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_pair_channel_branch_b","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_pair_channel_branch_b","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_growth_trichotomy"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.linearTrichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.linearTrichotomy","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L167-L209","doc":"A `LeviGrowthTrichotomy` with linearly growing condition number and\n`β = 1`.  `beta_upper` and `beta_lower` are the two halves of the\nlimsup; both reduce to the rpow-growth lemmas after splitting\n`κ^(1±ε) = κ · κ^(±ε)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.eventually_lt_rpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.eventually_lt_rpow","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L151-L159","doc":"**Eventually** `c < κ^e`, in the \"for all large κ\" form `beta_upper`\nneeds — `exists_large_rpow` gives one index, monotonicity of `x ↦ x^e`\nin the base extends it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_condNumber_degenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_condNumber_degenerate","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L139-L149","doc":"**Branch B fires**: under linear growth the Levi form degenerates.\n\nThis is the payoff — `branchB` is a field of the carrier, and this is\nthe first place in the corpus where its hypothesis is *derived* from the\ncondition number rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_condNumber_forces_beta_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.linear_condNumber_forces_beta_one","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L82-L137","doc":"**A linearly growing condition number forces `β = 1`** — branch B.\n\nThe dual of `bounded_condNumber_forces_beta_zero`, and the reason the\nmarginal window C is not where this channel lives.  If `C_L(κ) = A·κ`\neventually with `A > 0`, then no exponent below `1` can be an upper\nexponent: `beta_upper` at `ε = (1 - β)/2` would give `A·κ ≤ κ^s` with\n`s = (1+β)/2 < 1`, i.e. `A·κ^(1-s) ≤ 1` — but `κ^(1-s)` is unbounded.\n\nNote what is *not* needed: no lower bound on `β`, no fit, and no\nprecision claim.  `beta_mem` supplies `β ≤ 1` and this supplies `β ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.exists_large_rpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.exists_large_rpow","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_pair_channel_branch_b.lean#L68-L80","doc":"**Every positive level is eventually exceeded by `n^e`, `e > 0`** — the\none archimedean fact all three growth arguments below need, factored out\nso each of them is bookkeeping.  Returns an index that is also `≥ M`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}